# (tt, conc, kv) with --kv-bucket-width (default 4096, 0 disables), and the
# oracle prefers those tables, falling back to the 2D ones for older packs or
# when VLLM_EMULATOR_ORACLE_IGNORE_KV=1.  The 2D tables are still emitted
# unchanged, so an unpatched oracle reads a new pack exactly as before.
#
# Back-test replaying all 13 400 captured steps through the oracle and comparing
# against the measured latency of each step:
#
#     2D (tt, conc)        MAE 31.1%   median |err| 4.2%   prefill MAE 22.2%
#     3D (tt, conc, kv)    MAE 25.7%   median |err| 1.1%   prefill MAE 12.6%
#
